    "updated_at": "2025-08-20T07:22:11Z",
    "body": "The spec indeed covers this, especially after https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11515: see https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-worker's-lifetime . That added some discussion of bfcache specifically in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#note-worker-lifetime-terminology , although it still took me some time to figure out that workers whose owners are all inactive are suspendable, and thus [will be suspended](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#step-suspending-workers).\n\nI guess there is some ambiguity around the exact meaning of\n\n> ...the user agent suspends execution of script in _worker global scope_ until...\n\nand whether that allows or encourages the JS VM to pause mid-task, vs. just pausing the event loop. I'm not sure if we should add more here.",
