    "created_at": "2025-09-01T18:52:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-01T18:52:10Z",
    "body": "> ## Pause and resume them\n>\n> Chrome already does this with DedicatedWorkers although I don't think there is any spec. \"Pause\" here does not mean to pause the event loop, it means to pause the JS VM mid-task. This was necessary for DedicatedWorkers because there is no expectation of short-lived JS tasks, they are free continue without yielding.\n>\n> I don't know if there is any way express this kind of pausing in the spec.\n\n[...]\n\n> I guess there is some ambiguity around the exact meaning of:\n>> ...the user agent suspends execution of script in worker global scope until...\n\nI think some combination of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#immediately and https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#pause gives us what we want here—maybe we literally want to \"immediately pause\" the worker's event loop in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/C/#step-suspending-workers? @fergald, you said that Chromium already does this for dedicated workers, do you think it is feasible or compatible to do this with shared workers too?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
