    "created_at": "2026-03-10T03:30:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-10T03:30:22Z",
    "body": "Regarding the \"**lock-holding footgun**,\" I’d like to clarify my position. Since the extended lifetime is an explicit opt-in that cannot be changed once the SharedWorker has started, we should not see any unintended usage of this feature. Therefore, ensuring the safe implementation of SharedWorker logic remains the developer's responsibility. Furthermore, as ServiceWorkers can already hold WebLocks and create similar scenarios, I believe that introducing extended lifetimes for SharedWorkers does not significantly increase the overall risk.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
